# Prageeth Residences: Interactive 3D Tower (Google-Maps-style) (exact recreation prompt)

Build a single-page, cinematic **3D room-rental website** called **Prageeth Residences** for a beachfront tower in Negombo, Sri Lanka.

- **Scene:** a real-time 3D model of the tower stands on a beach with sea, palm trees, a road and low neighbouring buildings. The user can orbit, tilt, zoom and pan the camera like Google Maps 3D.
- **Floors:** hovering a floor highlights it; clicking selects it and the camera glides to that level. A frosted-glass `Choose your floor` card on the right shows the level, unit type, units available and rent.
- **Enter level:** pressing `Enter level N` flies the camera to that level's balcony, flashes through glass, and lands inside the room as a full-screen photo with hotspot pills, a `Level N` badge and a `Back to the tower` button.
- **Feel:** slow, smooth, luxury, golden light. Everything eases; nothing snaps.

Use one HTML file with plain CSS and vanilla JS. The ONLY library allowed is **three.js r160** (ES modules via an import map, pinned exactly):
```html
<script type="importmap">{"imports":{
 "three":"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.160.0/build/three.module.js",
 "three/addons/":"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.160.0/examples/jsm/"}}</script>
```
Reproduce every value, string and timing exactly. Implement in this **BUILD ORDER**, making sure each stage works before the next: (1) page, UI shell, poster; (2) 3D scene, tower, environment; (3) camera controls; (4) floor picking, highlight, card, rail; (5) availability, cutaway, units; (6) enter-level transition and interior view; (7) modal, phones, reduced motion.

